      "justification": "Core entity CRUD is cleanly separated, but the transaction read surface is crowded: filter, get, search_by_amount/category/month/payee, uncategorized, aggregate, summary_by_category/payee and query_run all return or summarize overlapping rows. The descriptions do draw boundaries (id vs name, month vs range, totals vs rows), which keeps it usable, but choosing among them still takes careful reading."
    },
    "naming_consistency": {
      "score": 3,
      "justification": "A strong and predictable actual_<resource>_<action> prefix runs throughout, which makes discovery easy. However the action segment mixes conventions: camelCase budget operations (getMonth, setAmount, holdForNextMonth) sit beside snake_case ones (get_all, updates_batch, list_available), and get_balance coexists with get_balance-style calls under a different casing scheme."
    },
    "tool_count_appropriateness": {
      "score": 2,
